-- title:
--   Injectivity of the Lubin–Tate coordinate on the Drinfeld deformation ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$, and a complete discrete valuation domain $W_0$ whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, together with a surjection $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal. Let $F_0$ be a commutative formal group law over $k$ satisfying `IsDrinfeldBasisAdic ⊥ q 0 0`, i.e. with the zero ideal installed as the ambient ideal, its $q$-th series is a unit multiple of its Drinfeld divisor at $(0,0)$. Let $R$ be a Noetherian local $W_0$-algebra, complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, with a surjection $\mathrm{res}_R : R \to k$ of kernel $\mathfrak m_R$ compatible with $\mathrm{res}_0$ on $W_0$; let $F$ be a commutative formal group law over $R$ whose coefficientwise image under $\mathrm{res}_R$ is $F_0$, and $x_0, x_1 \in \mathfrak m_R$ with $F.\mathrm{nthSeries}\,q$ a unit multiple of the Drinfeld divisor of $F$ at $(x_0,x_1)$ relative to $\mathfrak m_R$. Assume (`huniv`) that $(R, F, x_0, x_1)$ is universal among Artinian local $W_0$-algebras $T$ with residue map to $k$ compatible with $\mathrm{res}_0$, carrying a commutative formal group law $G$ reducing to $F_0$ and points $y_0, y_1 \in \mathfrak m_T$ with the same Drinfeld-divisor property: there is a unique $W_0$-algebra map $\varphi : R \to T$ over $k$ for which $F$ base-changes along $\varphi$ to some $F'$ admitting an isomorphism of laws $\psi : F' \to G$ whose series reduces to $X$ modulo $\mathfrak m_T$ and which carries $\varphi(x_0), \varphi(x_1)$ to $y_0, y_1$. Let further $F^u$ be a commutative formal group law over $W_0[[t]]$ reducing to $F_0$ along $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$ and satisfying (`hLT`) the corresponding universality without level data among such Artinian $T$. Then every $W_0$-algebra map $\varphi : W_0[[t]] \to R$ inducing $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$ on residues, along which $F^u$ base-changes to a law $F'$ isomorphic to $F$ by an isomorphism whose series reduces to $X$, is injective.
--
--   This is the dominance step in the theory of deformations of a one-dimensional formal group with Drinfeld level-$q$ structure: the Lubin–Tate coordinate $W_0[[t]] \to R$ classifying the underlying deformation has zero kernel. It feeds the determination of $R$ as a two-dimensional regular local ring, and thence the normality and reducedness statements for adic completions of modular curves of full level.
